{
  "_what": "Golden expectations for the drivers producer (SPEC-028). For each golden-fixture variant: the POSITIONAL driver evidence IntOGen's published compendium supports, within the COAD/READ (colorectal) cohort scope.",
  "_what_is_NOT_here": "No IntOGen payload beyond what our own assertion needs. IntOGen is CC0 and committing a slice WOULD be permitted (decision D-013) -- the fetch-to-gitignored-cache pattern is kept anyway, for consistency with the two licence-encumbered providers. The test proves these expectations against a locally fetched cache and SKIPs with a populate instruction when it is absent.",
  "_the_central_point": "`gene_is_driver_in_scope` is TRUE for all 20 entries. A gene-level driver signal over these variants is CONSTANT and therefore carries no information. All the discrimination is positional: 10 variants have a residue inside a significant domain/2D/3D cluster, 5 are in a driver gene with no positional support, and 5 are not missense. A gene being a driver does NOT make every variant in it a driver.",
  "_no_driver_call": "There is deliberately no expected `is_driver` per variant. This producer reports EVIDENCE. See contracts/driver_evidence.py.",
  "_id_namespace": "v01-v20 are the SAME variants as fixtures/variant_effect/variants_input.csv -- the same genomic facts seen by a different producer, not a colliding namespace. SPEC-016 requires disjoint IDs across fixture directories where the same id would mean DIFFERENT things; here it means the same thing, so reuse is correct and deliberate.",
